{
  "id": "ss.relic.crit",
  "name": "Hunter's eye",
  "description": "A compound eye as a clutch of thirteen hexagonal facets, each one a lit dome — a dusky violet cell with a paler crown set up-left — packed on a scalloped ink ground, the cluster tilted eight degrees and one facet short at the bottom so it is a grown thing and not a honeycomb logo. One facet up-right of centre burns coral with a soft coral bleed onto its neighbours: the ommatidium that found the seam in the target, which is what a fifteen-percent double hit is. Every facet is a lit dome rather than a dark cell with a bright rim, because a ring of bright around dark is an eye socket or a hole at this size and this icon is an eye that is looking, not one that is empty. The facets that face away from the light darken toward the lower right so the whole reads as one curved organ.",
